  "verbalization": "Divaricataester C is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and (1S,2R,7R,9S,10S)-6-acetyl-6'-methoxy-1'-methylspiro[4-oxa-12-azatricyclo[7.2.1.02,7]dodec-5-ene-10,3'-indole]-2'-one. These compounds are both implicated in the regulation of sialylation, a process that is critical for cell surface glycoconjugate formation and has been linked to various biological functions, including immune response and cell adhesion. The shared target of these compounds with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase suggests a potential mechanism by which Divaricataester C may exert its effects on SK-VLB, a cell line that may be sensitive to changes in sialylation. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Divaricataester C and SK-VLB through the modulation of sialyltransferase activity, which could influence cellular processes and potentially lead to therapeutic effects. The integration of multiple pathways and targets highlights the importance of sialylation in cellular function and suggests that Divaricataester C may act through a well-defined and biologically relevant mechanism.",
